Non-termination denotes $\bot$, and the least fixed point contains only what finitely many unfoldings determine.
For example, the factorial function is the least fixed point of $\lambda g. \lambda n. \mathsf {if} \, n = 0 \, \mathsf {then} \, 1 \, \mathsf {else} \, n \times \map g {n - 1}$.
{{qed}}
